Name the kext whose start is entered

The pair that matters is enter and leave.  Only leave was printed, so a kext
that hangs in its own start() is invisible: run-269 froze on apfs, and the only
way to tell was that some other kext's exit line was the last thing on the panel.
Print the identifier on the way in as well (no 0x%x here -- result is not set
yet), and every freeze names its kext directly.
---
diff --git a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
index d14d5c1..64ff31e 100644
--- a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
@@ -8197,6 +8197,12 @@ OSReturn
 OSKext::start(bool startDependenciesFlag)
 {
 	OSReturn                            result = kOSReturnError;
+
+	/* nio: the exit at finish: names the kext that came back.  A kext that
+	 * never comes back leaves nothing at all, which is how apfs looked for
+	 * three rounds.  This line is the other half of the pair. */
+	printf("nio: start> %s\n",
+	    (getIdentifierCString() != NULL) ? getIdentifierCString() : "(null)");
 	kern_return_t                       (* startfunc)(kmod_info_t *, void *);
 	unsigned int                        i, count;
 	void                              * kmodStartData = NULL;
